# Volkswagen Polo Mk3 (Typ 6N) three-door hatchback, 1994-2001.
#
# The rounded 1990s Polo: narrow grille between rectangular headlamps,
# body-coloured bumpers with a black rubbing strip, a single long door per
# side and a fixed rear quarter window. The pre-facelift 6N is modelled; the
# 6N2 facelift of February 2000 with clear-lens lamps is not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volkswagen_Polo_Mk3
#
# Dimensions 3.715 x 1.655 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.407 m (Wikipedia; the
# German infobox rounds the wheelbase to 2.400 m).
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a continental left-hand-drive
# three-door 6N, same body as the UK car; the detail image is a UK-registered
# 1998 Polo CL. All four images show the pre-facelift front end.
#
# Colours: no UK brochure or price list was read, so no factory name is
# claimed (grade d). Green, Red, Blue and Silver are plain colour names.
# Weights 10, 9, 8, 8, total 35, reflecting the Polo's UK volume in the 1990s,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 155 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 1,2.
# Dates 1994-2001 production, road tail staggered 2016-2019.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk3.dae. References: citycars/references/vw-polo-mk3/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0/4.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift 6N is modelled with UK amber front
# indicators from the CL detail image. Lens internals, grille slats and wheel
# ventilation holes are simplified; the aerial, rear wiper and model lettering
# are omitted at sprite scale.


obj=citycar
name=VWPoloMk3(Green)
copyright=JamesPetts

